{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1232528-charlatans-in-2e","id":1232528,"title":"Charlatans in 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-04T18:58:28-07:00","id":1232528,"title":"Charlatans in 2e","content":"I've been poking back and forth at the rules for 1e Charlatans in Autumn Nightmares vs. the rules for Gentry/Titles in the manuscript preview. Overall it seems like 2e wants the True Fae to be more background/final boss characters who rarely, if ever, visit Ironside in person if they could send a Huntsman instead, so Charlatans are probably less of a thing. But given that one of the Title write-ups is a Name exiled from Arcadia, the concept clearly isn't totally going away completely.<br /> <br /> Mostly I'm curious about the Name/Title system for 2e and what implications that has for Charlatans. The Man With The Ergot Smile is explicitly written up as a Name stripped of all Titles (which may be the only way the other Gentry were able to exile him from Arcadia in the first place). But assuming the &quot;dying while Ironside&quot; or &quot;connection to a mortal&quot; routes to becoming a Charlatan are still available, could just one of a True Fae's Titles be affected? Would that Title still be connected to the rest of their self on some level, or does catching human mean they're cut off? (And if they're cut off, does that mean this is one route another True Fae could take to swiping that Title for themself?) Or are Titles ultimately too ephemeral to become Charlatans, and only Names can survive Ironside well enough to transition?<br /> <br /> This ends up having a mechanical implication, since 2e Gentry know <i>all </i>the Contracts for one Regalia plus another Regalia per Title. Granted, Charlatans forget most of their Contracts -- but which ones they'd have access to in the first place depends on whether they could call upon a Regalia outside their own. (Example: A True Fae with three titles controls Jewels, Mirror, Sword and Steed. One of its titles, which controls Steed, is killed Ironside and is reborn a Charlatan. Is this possible? Does that Charlatan potentially remember only Steed Contracts, or could she also remember Contracts from the other Regalia? Conversely, do the other Titles lose access to Steed Contracts until they re-assimilate the Charlatan?)<br /> <br /> I'm curious what you all think/how you would approach the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T19:52:08-07:00","id":1232540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1232528-charlatans-in-2e#post1232528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been poking back and forth at the rules for 1e Charlatans in Autumn Nightmares vs. the rules for Gentry/Titles in the manuscript preview. Overall it seems like 2e wants the True Fae to be more background/final boss characters who rarely, if ever, visit Ironside in person if they could send a Huntsman instead, so Charlatans are probably less of a thing. But given that one of the Title write-ups is a Name exiled from Arcadia, the concept clearly isn't totally going away completely.<br /> <br /> Mostly I'm curious about the Name/Title system for 2e and what implications that has for Charlatans. The Man With The Ergot Smile is explicitly written up as a Name stripped of all Titles (which may be the only way the other Gentry were able to exile him from Arcadia in the first place). But assuming the &quot;dying while Ironside&quot; or &quot;connection to a mortal&quot; routes to becoming a Charlatan are still available, could just one of a True Fae's Titles be affected? Would that Title still be connected to the rest of their self on some level, or does catching human mean they're cut off? (And if they're cut off, does that mean this is one route another True Fae could take to swiping that Title for themself?) Or are Titles ultimately too ephemeral to become Charlatans, and only Names can survive Ironside well enough to transition?<br /> <br /> This ends up having a mechanical implication, since 2e Gentry know <i>all </i>the Contracts for one Regalia plus another Regalia per Title. Granted, Charlatans forget most of their Contracts -- but which ones they'd have access to in the first place depends on whether they could call upon a Regalia outside their own. (Example: A True Fae with three titles controls Jewels, Mirror, Sword and Steed. One of its titles, which controls Steed, is killed Ironside and is reborn a Charlatan. Is this possible? Does that Charlatan potentially remember only Steed Contracts, or could she also remember Contracts from the other Regalia? Conversely, do the other Titles lose access to Steed Contracts until they re-assimilate the Charlatan?)<br /> <br /> I'm curious what you all think/how you would approach the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, this was a snag and snarl for first edition too, with Equinox Road's introduction of Titles and Names clashing with Autumn Nightmares' more street level look at the Strangers. Just a note.<br /> <br /> Second, the main assumption has always been that singular Titles were the ones affected by the Charlatan-ization because Autumn Nightmares is concerned with the individual actors (and Actors) of a True Fae rather than their whole cast. It would effectively be cut off from the rest as though it were in Exile, since in effect that's exactly what's happening-it's caught in a Pledgeless Exile. Still, it's reclaimable, in that way any of those lost Titles are. Loyalists (and probably Huntsmen) have a lot of frying pans to handle asides from the Lost.<br /> <br /> Third, Names in Ironside are something of an actual grey area as far as precedent goes, since our only current example is <i>maybe</i> The Man with The Ergot Smile(more likely an Exile of some sort), but I would be more inclined to suggest that it's a rare instance of absolute dissolution. TO be operating as a Name is a <i>highly</i> vulnerable position, and with that precedence, it sets the stage for a Name going to Ironside being a risky-but-possibly alluring way of drawing another Stranger into a Legend with you, in which the Wyrd favors you-namely because in all honesty the Name wants to remain in Arcadia where it's safe for them but doing so encourages other Strangers to just let them Dwindle rather than jumping into a losing game. That sort of gamble makes the most sense if it entails dissolution. It also works for those Strangers who are the result of Becoming Nightmare, because they've already proven to be so vulnerable to reality that to be subjected to it full on again without a possible Madoka Rebellion style Witch-Reversal would metaphorically amount to be consumed by oblivion-and metaphor is as good as the real thing.<br /> <br /> Fourth, we really have no precedence of the relationship of Stranger's Regalia with how Charlatans work, but since a major part of the point is to somewhat-obscure the truth of them, the best argument is that their central Regalia plus the one tied to the Title that fell to Ironside act as ruling Regalia for them as much as each of the Seemings do, but the limitations otherwise do not quite manifest-Charlatans should stand a decent chance of always being excused as changelings, given the niche.<br /> <br /> Fifth, as regards to how the other titles act while that Charlatan Title is in the wild, well, yeah, it counts as a lost title, so the effects they'd normally have for it's presence are lost.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut that's just, like, my take man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T22:18:47-07:00","id":1232558,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Sean! Good to know that the discontinuity between AN and ER isn't all in my head.<br /> <br /> Is there any hard-and-fast rule for distinguishing between Exiles and exiled Charlatans? I supposed the former are usually down to Names while the latter could be Titles, and of course Charlatans have the amnesia thing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T23:08:31-07:00","id":1232562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1232528-charlatans-in-2e?p=1232558#post1232558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, Sean! Good to know that the discontinuity between AN and ER isn't all in my head.<br /> <br /> Is there any hard-and-fast rule for distinguishing between Exiles and exiled Charlatans? I supposed the former are usually down to Names while the latter could be Titles, and of course Charlatans have the amnesia thing...</div> </div> </div> </div>Been a while since I've read Autumn Nightmares, but as a general rule, Exiles are basically just Titles(or Names, rarely) that are ousted from Arcadia but aren't yet Charlatans, either by enforced Pledges of other True Fae or as a means of escaping the consequences of a Legend. They are still True Fae, in all effects(I forgot some of the distinctions), including the time limit in Ironside. Charlatans are those true Fae who are diminished but have a means of operating in Ironside as a result of a banishment pledge, death in the mortal world, or attachment to the mortal world(ie, investing some of that Title into reality).<br /> <br /> Names really don't casually appear in Ironside, because it is a really dangerous prospect for them to be in and it makes sense, even by the dream logic of the Strangers, to play the defensive game and hope that those damn changelings and hobgoblins under you are actually good for something. It would be a bold risk for a truly vulnerable Stranger to present themselves to Ironside, and as mentioned, the most problem result of that is absolute dissolution BARRING any sensible narrative caveat that would earn the appropriate drama of a former-changeling turning back into said changeling, but it had <i>better</i> be a damn setup, and there's no rules of precedent concerning that angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T13:57:24-07:00","id":1232696,"title":"","content":"Aha! I came away with the impression that an exiled Title automatically became a Charlatan, hence my confusion. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}